00:10:53.765 --> 00:10:55.379
"you got this big house, like,

00:10:55.379 --> 00:10:58.112
"why can't you afford a
selfie stick or a tripod?"

00:10:58.112 --> 00:11:00.628
Well, I actually do have
a tripod right there,

00:11:00.628 --> 00:11:04.033
but a lot of things people engage better,

00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:06.146
I've tested it, people
want to know, it's like,

00:11:06.146 --> 00:11:07.835
having a face-to-face conversation.

00:11:07.835 --> 00:11:11.441
So, make sure social media
is not too stiff and stuffy,

00:11:11.441 --> 00:11:13.013
you know? Make sure,

00:11:13.013 --> 00:11:15.807
like, The Office TV show, some of you saw,

00:11:15.807 --> 00:11:17.535
I know Dwight Schrute, Rain Wilson,

00:11:17.535 --> 00:11:19.141
he was here at the house, I don't know,

00:11:19.141 --> 00:11:21.142
a week or two ago and we
were talking about how

00:11:21.142 --> 00:11:23.502
The Office, they would use these cameras

00:11:23.502 --> 00:11:26.537
which made it feel like you
were in the actual office

00:11:26.537 --> 00:11:29.125
with Steve Carrel and
you know, Dwight Schrute

00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:30.475
and all these funny guys.

00:11:30.475 --> 00:11:32.099
And so, it upped their ratings,

00:11:32.099 --> 00:11:34.656
they did 202 episodes.

00:11:34.656 --> 00:11:38.075
So, whether it's TV,
whether it's Instagram,

00:11:38.075 --> 00:11:41.136
even your video, even your
entrepreneurial growth

00:11:41.136 --> 00:11:45.706
can be fueled by this reality
slash lifestyle branding.

00:11:45.706 --> 00:11:48.721
So, I mean, you know,

00:11:48.721 --> 00:11:50.819
I got YouTube videos I've done,

00:11:50.819 --> 00:11:54.812
a lot of views, 60 million
views that were done like this.

00:11:54.812 --> 00:11:58.998
And how was that, how did I kind
of come to that realization?

00:11:58.998 --> 00:12:02.373
Well, it was by following
people straight to the top,

00:12:02.373 --> 00:12:04.806
even if you look at a
lot of these big people,

00:12:04.806 --> 00:12:07.578
whether it's, you know, Taylor Swift,

00:12:07.578 --> 00:12:10.377
or Ariana Grande has a big following,

00:12:10.377 --> 00:12:13.012
and you look at the
engagement of which pictures

00:12:13.012 --> 00:12:15.743
and which videos get the most
engagement on their social,

00:12:15.743 --> 00:12:18.395
that's information gathering sessions.

00:12:18.395 --> 00:12:20.176
You sit there and you stare
at it and you're like,

00:12:20.176 --> 00:12:22.003
"Wait a sec, that
picture that's all formal

00:12:22.003 --> 00:12:24.010
"with the photographer that's all stiff,

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.033
"that one got, you know, 50,000 likes

00:12:26.033 --> 00:12:27.385
"and this one where it's just like,

00:12:27.385 --> 00:12:30.023
"her like, with a camera
going like, what's up!

00:12:30.023 --> 00:12:31.284
"That one did 75,000."

00:12:31.284 --> 00:12:33.768
Boom, clue revealed,
clue reveals the answer

00:12:33.768 --> 00:12:35.648
right there to you so...

00:12:35.648 --> 00:12:37.469
- So, I have a couple quick
thoughts on social media

00:12:37.469 --> 00:12:39.487
that I wanted to share
and how to have success.

00:12:39.487 --> 00:12:41.698
Number one is you have
to define your outcome.

00:12:41.698 --> 00:12:43.549
It's important to know
what you want out of this.

00:12:43.549 --> 00:12:45.714
Are you trying to build a personal brand?

00:12:45.714 --> 00:12:48.452
Are you trying to sell
your product or service?

00:12:48.452 --> 00:12:50.850
Are you trying to just
have a form of escape

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.912
just to get away from your busy life

00:12:52.912 --> 00:12:54.399
and you want to connect with your friends?

00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:57.135
Understanding why you're on the platform

00:12:57.135 --> 00:13:00.030
will help you devise a strategy to win.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.169
Number two is find your voice.

00:13:02.169 --> 00:13:04.420
It's really important
that you understand that

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.140
there is nobody else like you.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.585
There's a lot of other people out there,

00:13:07.585 --> 00:13:09.934
they have their own
opinions, their own voices,

00:13:09.934 --> 00:13:11.364
but you're not going to succeed

00:13:11.364 --> 00:13:13.932
by just being a copy of somebody else.

00:13:13.932 --> 00:13:16.258
Your ultimate success will come by you

00:13:16.258 --> 00:13:18.478
finding your own voice
and putting out content

00:13:18.478 --> 00:13:19.988
that you resonate with that

00:13:19.988 --> 00:13:22.691
other people aren't
saying those exact things.

00:13:22.691 --> 00:13:24.420
And so at the beginning, this is hard.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.040
At the beginning, you don't
know what your voice is,

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.309
at the beginning, you're still
trying to figure it all out.

00:13:28.309 --> 00:13:29.861
And so, I think it's actually okay

00:13:29.861 --> 00:13:31.248
to copy people at the start.

00:13:31.248 --> 00:13:33.824
It's okay to copy somebody's
style of making videos,

00:13:33.824 --> 00:13:36.097
or making tweets, or
making Instagram pictures.

00:13:36.097 --> 00:13:37.425
It's okay to copy.

00:13:37.425 --> 00:13:40.197
And in that process, you
learn about yourself.

00:13:40.197 --> 00:13:41.587
You need to understand, though,

00:13:41.587 --> 00:13:43.245
that your ultimate success won't come

00:13:43.245 --> 00:13:44.759
by copying somebody else.

00:13:44.759 --> 00:13:46.733
You will never be massively successful

00:13:46.733 --> 00:13:49.897
by just being a junior
version of somebody else

00:13:49.897 --> 00:13:52.881
so, a lot of people copy my
video style, as an example.

00:13:52.881 --> 00:13:54.435
They make their own top 10 rules

00:13:54.435 --> 00:13:56.145
or their own versions of what I'm doing.

00:13:56.145 --> 00:13:57.588
And that's okay, it doesn't bother me.

00:13:57.588 --> 00:13:59.535
They're never going to have the success

00:13:59.535 --> 00:14:01.767
that I'm having if
they're just copying me.

00:14:01.767 --> 00:14:04.632
But what it allow you to
do, by coping those people,

00:14:04.632 --> 00:14:07.933
is then see, hmm, I like that,

00:14:07.933 --> 00:14:10.115
I like what Evan's doing,
I like what Gary's doing,

00:14:10.115 --> 00:14:12.752
I like what Jimmy is doing,
I like what Susan is doing.

00:14:12.752 --> 00:14:14.818
But I want to twist it up a little bit.

00:14:14.818 --> 00:14:16.754
And that's where you're
going to have success.

00:14:16.754 --> 00:14:19.319
When you take what is
working for somebody else,

00:14:19.319 --> 00:14:21.575
and then you twist it
and add some flavor to it

00:14:21.575 --> 00:14:23.409
that only you can add.

00:14:23.409 --> 00:14:25.668
Because you can never out-Evan Evan,

00:14:25.668 --> 00:14:27.924
and I can never out-you you.

00:14:27.924 --> 00:14:30.481
So, go be you! That's
how you're going to win.

00:14:30.481 --> 00:14:31.828
You need to find your voice.

00:14:31.828 --> 00:14:33.532
And number three is is be prolific.

00:14:33.532 --> 00:14:35.170
It's important that if you were trying

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:36.267
to achieve a real outcome,

00:14:36.267 --> 00:14:37.249
and you're trying to build a brand,

00:14:37.249 --> 00:14:38.230
you're trying to sell product,

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:41.264
that you are prolific in
the creation of the content.

00:14:41.264 --> 00:14:42.879
You're not going to get really great at it

00:14:42.879 --> 00:14:44.420
if you're doing something once a week.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.315
You're just not going to
get really good at it.

00:14:46.315 --> 00:14:48.085
Try learning anything once a week

00:14:48.085 --> 00:14:49.759
without practicing in between,

00:14:49.759 --> 00:14:51.571
you're never going to
get really good at it.

00:14:51.571 --> 00:14:53.238
If you're trying to pick up salsa dancing,

00:14:53.238 --> 00:14:56.017
or you want to learn Spanish,
or you want to play the piano,

00:14:56.017 --> 00:14:57.741
if you're only doing it once a week,

00:14:57.741 --> 00:15:00.553
you're never going to get really,
really, really good at it.

00:15:00.553 --> 00:15:01.900
You need to be more prolific.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.874
The quantity leads to the quality.

00:15:03.874 --> 00:15:06.529
The practice leads to you
getting good at something,

00:15:06.529 --> 00:15:08.216
and so, back to number one,

00:15:08.216 --> 00:15:10.982
if you have you a goal, if
you have a business objective,

00:15:10.982 --> 00:15:12.156
and this is important to you

00:15:12.156 --> 00:15:13.390
that you have success with it,

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.454
then you need to dedicate
time for you to learn it,

00:15:16.454 --> 00:15:19.452
to get good at it, to practice,
to practice, to practice.

00:15:19.452 --> 00:15:22.735
To be prolific, so that
you can find your voice,

00:15:22.735 --> 00:15:26.568
and create content that
really touches people.

00:15:28.601 --> 00:15:30.932
So, those are my thoughts on social media,

00:15:30.932 --> 00:15:33.008
those are some of the thoughts
of the experts in the field.

00:15:33.008 --> 00:15:36.231
I made this video because
the Darth Reaper asked me to.

00:15:36.231 --> 00:15:37.513
So, if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:15:37.513 --> 00:15:39.444
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:15:39.444 --> 00:15:41.673
leave it down in the comments
and I'll see what I can do.

00:15:41.673 --> 00:15:42.960
I'm also curious to figure out

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.953
what did you like most about this video?

00:15:44.953 --> 00:15:47.100
What lesson are you going
to immediately apply

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.881
to your life, to your
business, after watching this?

00:15:49.881 --> 00:15:51.524
And why are you on social?

00:15:51.524 --> 00:15:53.968
What is your outcome,
what is your objective?

00:15:53.968 --> 00:15:56.899
Are you doing it for personal
development, to try to learn?

00:15:56.899 --> 00:15:58.346
Are you trying to build
a brand and sell product?

00:15:58.346 --> 00:16:00.067
Is it just an escape from your busy life

00:16:00.067 --> 00:16:01.285
and you want to be entertained?

00:16:01.285 --> 00:16:02.735
Super curious to figure that out.

00:16:02.735 --> 00:16:04.961
Leave it in the comments, I'm
