00:16:21.847 --> 00:16:23.776
and whatever your one word is,

00:16:23.776 --> 00:16:27.943
much love, have an amazing
day. I'll see you soon.

00:16:33.522 --> 00:16:34.958
- It's just not how, what was the ROY

00:16:34.958 --> 00:16:36.460
being on the cover of Ink?

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:38.112
- Great question.
- You know, to me,

00:16:38.112 --> 00:16:39.799
the answer is it's got to be something,

00:16:39.799 --> 00:16:41.647
it's a lot of impressions and awareness

00:16:41.647 --> 00:16:43.913
that may get them into
the rabbit hole of me.

00:16:43.913 --> 00:16:45.844
They saw me at the
airport, they saw the Ink,

00:16:45.844 --> 00:16:47.983
they Google me, they read my Wikipedia,

00:16:47.983 --> 00:16:50.282
they follow me on
Twitter, seven days later,

00:16:50.282 --> 00:16:51.711
I put out a good slideshare,

00:16:51.711 --> 00:16:54.033
nine days later, I ask
them to buy the book

00:16:54.033 --> 00:16:55.464
from a right hook on Twitter.

00:16:55.464 --> 00:16:57.551
They buy it, ROY to Ink.

00:16:57.551 --> 00:16:59.276
But how you're going to quantify that

00:16:59.276 --> 00:17:01.597
is insanity, and so I think social media

00:17:01.597 --> 00:17:04.468
has been asked to create an ROY

00:17:04.468 --> 00:17:06.746
that every other medium hasn't

00:17:06.746 --> 00:17:09.881
or hasn't since they've been accepted.

00:17:09.881 --> 00:17:12.060
Right? Television went through this.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.592
In the '50s and '60s, wait a minute,

00:17:13.592 --> 00:17:15.761
this TV thing, what's the ROY,

00:17:15.761 --> 00:17:18.409
we know what radio and print does.

00:17:18.409 --> 00:17:20.084
So, it's the same old
game, this is historic.

00:17:20.084 --> 00:17:21.707
I mean, we can be having this meeting,

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:24.269
I wish I was older, and I
wished that I was on the scene

00:17:24.269 --> 00:17:26.853
back in '95, six, seven, when
I talked about e-commerce

00:17:26.853 --> 00:17:28.242
because all the same questions.

00:17:28.242 --> 00:17:30.452
How are you going to compete
with Walmart and K-Mart

00:17:30.452 --> 00:17:31.792
and JC Penney's?

00:17:31.792 --> 00:17:34.959
And Barnes and Nobles and
Borders and Walden Books,

00:17:34.959 --> 00:17:36.283
how is this Amazon thing going to compete,

00:17:36.283 --> 00:17:38.875
I was laughing at people to the notion,

00:17:38.875 --> 00:17:41.392
and clearly that's played out
over the last two decades.

00:17:41.392 --> 00:17:43.775
I think we'll look back at what's the...

00:17:43.775 --> 00:17:46.569
The ROY of anything that
gets in front of the consumer

00:17:46.569 --> 00:17:47.786
where they actually spend their time,

00:17:47.786 --> 00:17:50.692
here's what I know: everybody
who's watching right now,

00:17:50.692 --> 00:17:52.792
they do this for a living.

00:17:52.792 --> 00:17:55.153
And if you don't know how
to get into this screen

00:17:55.153 --> 00:17:57.975
and storytell about what
you do for a living,

00:17:57.975 --> 00:17:59.125
you're out.

00:17:59.125 --> 00:18:02.152
Social networks control
an enormous percentage

00:18:02.152 --> 00:18:03.457
of that consumption.

00:18:03.457 --> 00:18:06.141
If you don't know how to
storytell in a screen economy

00:18:06.141 --> 00:18:09.371
in 2014, I think you're really
playing Russian Roulette

00:18:09.371 --> 00:18:10.935
with your advertising dollars.

00:18:10.935 --> 00:18:12.448
- You're going to have people around you

00:18:12.448 --> 00:18:13.966
in your organization,

00:18:13.966 --> 00:18:16.280
and/or you're going to get emails back

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:19.393
saying, oh, this doesn't work,
or this is a waste of time.

00:18:19.393 --> 00:18:22.405
Okay? You're also going to
have people tell you back off,

00:18:22.405 --> 00:18:25.010
okay, this is not
wanted, or don't spam me,

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.176
or you sent me the
wrong, I don't need this,

00:18:27.176 --> 00:18:28.847
why'd you send this to me?

00:18:28.847 --> 00:18:31.194
This is exactly what happens to all people

00:18:31.194 --> 00:18:33.008
that are trying to get attention.

00:18:33.008 --> 00:18:35.155
When you get attention at the right level,

00:18:35.155 --> 00:18:37.005
the first thing that's
going to happen to you

00:18:37.005 --> 00:18:38.910
is you're going to get criticism.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:41.474
You want to push through the criticism

00:18:41.474 --> 00:18:44.883
until you get admiration, you
want to push through more.

00:18:44.883 --> 00:18:46.397
It's not any different.

00:18:46.397 --> 00:18:49.464
Facebook, Twitter, YouTube,
social media is no different

00:18:49.464 --> 00:18:51.428
than me knocking on a door,

00:18:51.428 --> 00:18:53.406
saying, hey, I want to sell you a product.

00:18:53.406 --> 00:18:55.442
You're going to have people
slamming the door in your face.

00:18:55.442 --> 00:18:57.086
The next question go-to,
they're going to say,

00:18:57.086 --> 00:18:59.655
get out of my neighborhood,
what are you doing here?

00:18:59.655 --> 00:19:03.509
If you stop because of this suppression,

00:19:03.509 --> 00:19:05.633
this stop on you, if you stop

00:19:05.633 --> 00:19:09.039
because people are asking
you to stop, you're done.

00:19:09.039 --> 00:19:11.806
So, the same thing
happens with social media.

00:19:11.806 --> 00:19:13.242
Look, when you tweet,

00:19:13.242 --> 00:19:16.013
or when you put an entry into Facebook,

00:19:16.013 --> 00:19:19.206
the way to take that and
make it unique, okay,

00:19:19.206 --> 00:19:20.798
and not spammy,

00:19:20.798 --> 00:19:25.034
and not bother people
is to personalize it.

00:19:25.034 --> 00:19:26.985
So, consider the people that you've been

00:19:26.985 --> 00:19:29.215
trying to sell products
to, not just your friends.

00:19:29.215 --> 00:19:30.399
Let's say there was a plumber

00:19:30.399 --> 00:19:31.712
you were trying to sell a truck to.

00:19:31.712 --> 00:19:34.392
You would want to email
the plumber and say,

00:19:34.392 --> 00:19:37.101
Mr. Plumber, I just got a hold of a site

00:19:37.101 --> 00:19:39.932
of a sales trainer that
can increase your sales

00:19:39.932 --> 00:19:42.355
at your business, Mr. Plumber.

00:19:42.355 --> 00:19:45.044
And I wanted to make sure you
have the information there,

00:19:45.044 --> 00:19:47.319
I thought of you when I
saw this, and by the way,

00:19:47.319 --> 00:19:49.114
I could win $10,000.

00:19:49.114 --> 00:19:51.093
And so, could any of your employees

00:19:51.093 --> 00:19:53.518
as well as getting
hooked up with a guy that

00:19:53.518 --> 00:19:56.031
can increase your sales in this economy

00:19:56.031 --> 00:19:57.057
and I thought of you.

00:19:57.057 --> 00:19:58.407
So, you got to personalize it

00:19:58.407 --> 00:19:59.754
so that it's not spammy.

00:19:59.754 --> 00:20:01.736
You can't just keep using that one message

00:20:01.736 --> 00:20:03.389
we sent you yesterday which was,

00:20:03.389 --> 00:20:05.965
I can win $10,000 and so can you!

00:20:05.965 --> 00:20:08.690
Look, that's spammy, that's
why people say that's spammy,

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:10.539
you have to personalize it.

00:20:10.539 --> 00:20:12.892
- Do this with heart.

00:20:12.892 --> 00:20:16.980
You can't survive doing
this if your art isn't real,

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.560
if your heart isn't in the work,

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:19.613
'cause you won't get up in the morning

00:20:19.613 --> 00:20:20.893
and be motivated for it,

00:20:20.893 --> 00:20:22.905
you won't be excited about it.

00:20:22.905 --> 00:20:26.687
You have to have at the base
of all that you're posting,

00:20:26.687 --> 00:20:29.024
if people can tell that you care,

00:20:29.024 --> 00:20:30.432
you'll be followed.

00:20:30.432 --> 00:20:32.692
If people can tell that you care about

00:20:32.692 --> 00:20:34.685
values and humanity

00:20:34.685 --> 00:20:36.952
and the philosophy of living a good life

00:20:36.952 --> 00:20:39.702
and taking care of other
people, respecting other people,

00:20:39.702 --> 00:20:40.627
you'll be followed.

00:20:40.627 --> 00:20:42.617
You could become a caustic hater

00:20:42.617 --> 00:20:44.544
and maybe you'll gather a couple people,

00:20:44.544 --> 00:20:46.727
but you're never going
to get millions of people

00:20:46.727 --> 00:20:49.085
and if you do, you'll burn out your soul

00:20:49.085 --> 00:20:51.059
because nobody wants to live a life

00:20:51.059 --> 00:20:53.382
where they're just
criticizing and being a jerk.

00:20:53.382 --> 00:20:56.744
Be the positive thought
leader in whatever you do.

00:20:56.744 --> 00:20:59.854
Be the most caring. Be
the most consistent.

00:20:59.854 --> 00:21:01.523
Be the person who shows up.

00:21:01.523 --> 00:21:03.001
And if you'll just show up every day

00:21:03.001 --> 00:21:05.050
with the intention to
capture one unique moment,

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:07.310
one unique lesson, one unique story,

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:09.002
one unique quote, one unique picture,

00:21:09.002 --> 00:21:10.535
one unique video, whatever it is for you

00:21:10.535 --> 00:21:11.725
and your favorite medium,

00:21:11.725 --> 00:21:13.702
capture one thing every single day.

00:21:13.702 --> 00:21:15.726
You'll be fully energized with your life

00:21:15.726 --> 00:21:17.443
'cause life won't just be work anymore,

00:21:17.443 --> 00:21:18.835
it's art.

